note S4 empty text (`text e ""`, length 0) as a `view uchar *` argument (spec 6, erratum E2): its count is
note the number 0, never a count register. x = 7 is live in the register the old lowering read as the
note count. Checks: len through a parameter, through an inline parameter, len e itself, part e 0 0 and a
note 0-byte write. Exit 0 when every check holds, else the failing check's number.
om2
text e ""
fn plen v view uchar * to ulong
ret len v
end
fn ilen v view uchar * to ulong inline
ret len v
end
fn main to int
x = ulong 7
if ne plen e 0
ret 1
end
if ne ilen e 0
ret 2
end
if ne len e 0
ret 3
end
if ne plen part e 0 0 0
ret 4
end
n = write int 1 e ulong 0 ulong 0
if ne n 0
ret 5
end
ret int sub x 7
end
